# `workflow/` — Declarative pipeline

## Authority

The root [`README.md`](../README.md) contract defines canonical input and output
homes. Local [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) defines execution constraints.

```
workflow/
├── config.yaml   # DAG selectors/topology only
├── rules/        # Snakemake DAG declarations
├── scripts/      # thin Snakemake adapters
└── profiles/     # executor/scheduler/container/resource policy
```

`conf/config.yaml` owns scientific parameters. `conf/catalog.yaml` owns logical
dataset-to-path bindings. `workflow/config.yaml` may select a catalog key and
enable DAG branches, but must not duplicate dataset paths, scientific values, or
executor resource settings.

## Adding a stage

1. Implement and test reusable behavior in `src/`.
2. Add a thin `workflow/scripts/` adapter that consumes declared Snakemake
   inputs/configuration, calls `src/`, and writes only declared outputs.
3. Add a rule with complete inputs, outputs, parameters, logs, and environment.
4. Classify each output using the root contract: disposable scratch in
   `data/interim/`, reusable data in `data/processed/`, terminal QC/figures/tables
   in `results/`.
5. Dry-run and build the named target; verify provenance and failure behavior.

```bash
snakemake -n <target>
snakemake --cores 1 <target>
snakemake --list
```
{% if compute_backend == "slurm" %}
On HPC, use `snakemake --profile workflow/profiles/slurm`; do not run analysis
Python directly on a login node.
{% endif -%}


